Now I see the key part. In `theme_format_append_next`:

```c
chr = **format;
if ((chr == '$' || chr == '%') &&
    (*format)[1] == '\0') {
    /* last char, always append */
    g_string_append_c(str, chr);
    (*format)++;
    return;
}
```

This handles the case where `$` or `%` is the last character. But the vulnerability says "parsing does not stop on a lone tag escape in the C file". Let me look at the `expand_escape` function and how the theme file is parsed. Let me look at the theme file parsing code.

